# Product Overview

**SatuKas** is a comprehensive personal finance management web application built with Next.js. It helps users track their expenses, manage budgets, and gain insights into their financial habits through an intuitive dashboard interface.

**Tagline**: "Satu tempat untuk semua kebutuhan finansial Anda."

## Core Features

- **Multi-Book Management**

  - Users can create multiple separate accounting books within a single account
  - Supports personal finance, side jobs, organizations, and group finances
  - Each book has its own Chart of Accounts (COA), transactions, and reports

- **Financial Management**

  - Transaction entry and tracking (expense, income, transfer, saving, investment, debt, etc.)
  - Chart of Accounts (COA) management
  - Financial reports (Journal, Ledger, Balance Sheet)
  - Transaction history and reconciliation

- **User Management**

  - Secure authentication system (login, register, email verification)
  - Password recovery (forgot/reset password)
  - User profile and account settings
  - Workspace management (books and organizations)

- **Dashboard & UI**
  - Responsive layout with dark/light theme support
  - Multi-language support (Indonesian/English)
  - Interactive financial insights and charts
  - Modern, clean interface built with Shadcn UI

## Architecture & Tech Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router)
- **Language**: TypeScript
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS
- **UI Components**: Radix UI, Shadcn UI, Custom components
- **State Management**: React Query (TanStack Query)
- **Form Handling**: React Hook Form + Zod
- **HTTP Client**: Axios
- **Internationalization**: next-intl
- **Theme**: next-themes
- **Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library

## Project Structure

- **Single Frontend Application**: This is a standalone Next.js application (not part of a monorepo)
- **Component Organization**:
  - `components/ui/` - Base UI components (Shadcn UI)
  - `components/shared/` - Shared components across modules
  - `components/module/` - Feature-specific components (auth, book, coa, transaction, etc.)
  - `components/layout/` - Layout components
  - `components/page/` - Page-level components
- **Services**: API services organized by domain (AuthService, BookService, CoaService, TransactionService, etc.)
- **Hooks**: Custom React hooks organized by module
- **Types**: TypeScript types separated by API and client-side types

